This example demonstrates how to create a total ordering of events across machines using vector clocks without shared time or message exchange. Each machine maintains its own logical clock and exchanges vector timestamps to maintain global consistency. The `happensBefore` method determines the causal relationship between events, ensuring a consistent total order regardless of network delays or machine clock drift.

