When you run this program, it will serve files from the directory where the binary is executed. For example:
- Accessing `http://localhost:8080/index.html` will serve the `index.html` file in that directory.
- Accessing `http://localhost:8080/subdir/file.txt` will serve `subdir/file.txt`.

The server handles all standard HTTP methods (GET, HEAD) and automatically sets appropriate Content-Type headers based on file extensions.

