The `runtime_borrow_checker` is a nightly-only feature in Rust that allows you to check borrow rules at runtime (rather than compile-time). Here's a quick example of how to use it:

```rust
#![feature(runtime_borrow_checker)]

use std::mem;

fn main() {
    let mut x = 5;
    let y = &mut x; // This is normally checked at compile time

    // Runtime check
    if mem::needs_drop::<&mut i32>() {
        println!("Borrow checker active");
    }

    *y += 1;
    println!("x is now {}", x);
}
```

