**Note:** This example focuses on safety (ensuring only one client holds the lock at any time) but does not fully address liveness in the presence of network partitions or crashes without additional mechanisms like lease-based locking. For a complete solution that also addresses liveness under failure scenarios, more sophisticated techniques (e.g., heartbeat-based lease renewal, session management) are required.

### Prerequisites

1. **Go Environment**: Ensure you have Go installed.
2. **Etcd**: You need an etcd cluster running. For simplicity, you can run a single-node etcd instance locally for testing purposes. Follow the [official installation guide](https://etcd.io/docs/v3.5/install/) if you haven't set it up yet.

