### Bottom Line

- **You cannot safely give untrusted code *full* raw hardware access while guaranteeing escape‑proofness.** Doing so would defeat any confinement mechanism because the very act of controlling hardware implies the ability to subvert those mechanisms.
- The pattern above—**privileged wrapper + well‑defined, audited API + strict class‑loader permissions**—is the industry‑standard approach for safely executing untrusted code that needs limited hardware interaction.

