   - Potentially throttling application memory allocation if it detects that upcoming GC cycles might exceed the maximum pause time.

5. **Disabling Deterministic Mode**: Once the deterministic requirements are no longer needed (e.g., at the end of a critical section of code), `disableDeterministicMode()` can be called to return the garbage collector to its default behavior, which might offer better overall throughput or memory usage efficiency outside of real-time constraints.

