The `Write` method increments the counter based on node contributions. It uses a sequence number to prevent duplicates and updates either upper or lower bounds.

```go
func (p *PNCounter) Write(seq uint64, nodeID uint64) {
    index, exists := p.nodes[nodeID]
    if !exists {
        // New node; add new entries with the current seq as both up and lo
        p.up = append(p.up, seq)
        p.lo = append(p.lo, seq)
        p.nodes[nodeID] = len(p.up) - 1
        return
    }

    // Existing node; increment based on whether we're updating up or lo
    if p.up[index] < seq {
        p.up[index] = seq
    }
    if p.lo[index] < seq {
        p.lo[index] = seq
    }
}
```

