### 🧩 1. A Safe, Exception-Free JSON Parser (in pseudocode)

A common way to avoid exceptions is to use explicit error handling (`Result`/`Either` types) and make the parser **partial**—it only succeeds on *valid* input. If you want *zero* exceptions, the parser must handle all inputs without crashing (e.g., no out-of-bounds access, no null dereference).

Here’s a minimal recursive-descent parser in Rust-ish pseudocode:

```rust
enum JsonValue {
    Null,
    Bool(bool),
    Number(f64),
    String(String),
    Array(Vec<JsonValue>),
    Object(BTreeMap<String, JsonValue>),
}

struct Parser<'a> {
    input: &'a [u8],
    pos: usize,
}

impl<'a> Parser<'a> {
    fn parse(&mut self) -> Result<JsonValue, &'static str> {
        self.skip_whitespace();
        if self.pos >= self.input.len() { 
            return Err("Unexpected end of input"); 
        }
        let ch = self.input[self.pos] as char;
        match ch {
            'n' => self.parse_null(),
            't' | 'f' => self.parse_bool(),
            '"' => self.parse_string(),
            '[' => self.parse_array(),
            '{' => self.parse_object(),
            '0'..='9' | '-' => self.parse_number(),
            _ => Err("Unexpected character"),
        }
    }

    fn skip_whitespace(&mut self) {
        while self.pos < self.input.len() && 
              matches!(self.input[self.pos] as char, ' ' | '\n' | '\t' | '\r') {
            self.pos += 1;
        }
    }

    // Parse `null`
    fn parse_null(&mut self) -> Result<JsonValue, &'static str> {
        if self.input.get(self.pos..self.pos+4) == Some(b"null") {
            self.pos += 4;
            Ok(JsonValue::Null)
        } else {
            Err("Expected 'null'")
        }
    }

    // Similar safe implementations for `parse_bool`, `parse_string`, etc.
    // Each uses bounds-checked array access (`get()`) instead of direct indexing
}
```

✅ **Safety features**:
- Use `input.get(index..)` to avoid out-of-bounds panics.
- All error paths return `Err(...)` instead of panicking.
- Recursive descent ensures all code paths are explicit.

