The most common built‑in way to get an LRU cache in modern Java is to use:

1. **Guava Cache** (`com.google.common.cache.CacheBuilder`)  
2. **Caffeine** (a high‑performance fork of Guava’s cache)  
3. Or manually build one with `LinkedHashMap`

### 1. Using LinkedHashMap (no external dependencies)

You can subclass `java.util.LinkedHashMap` to get a simple LRU cache:

```java
import java.util.LinkedHashMap;
import java.util.Map;

public class LRUCache<K, V> extends LinkedHashMap<K, V> {
    private final int maxSize;

    public LRUCache(int maxSize) {
        super(maxSize, 0.75f, true); // accessOrder = true → LRU
        this.maxSize = maxSize;
    }

    @Override
    protected boolean removeEldestEntry(Map.Entry<K, V> eldest) {
        return size() > maxSize;   // evict when over capacity
    }

    // Optional: convenience methods
    public V getOrDefault(K key, V defaultValue) {
        V value = super.get(key);
        return (value != null || containsKey(key)) ? value : defaultValue;
    }
}
```

Usage:

```java
public static void main(String[] args) {
    LRUCache<String, String> cache = new LRUCache<>(3);

    cache.put("A", "Apple");
    cache.put("B", "Banana");
    cache.put("C", "Cherry");

    System.out.println(cache); // {A=Apple, B=Banana, C=Cherry}

    // Access A → moves it to end (most recently used)
    cache.get("A");

    cache.put("D", "Date"); // evicts "B" (least recently used)
    System.out.println(cache); // {A=Apple, C=Cherry, D=Date}
}
```

### 2. Using Google Guava Cache

If you’re open to dependencies, Guava is a great option:

```xml
<!-- pom.xml -->
<dependency>
    <groupId>com.google.guava</groupId>
    <artifactId>guava</artifactId>
    <version>33.4.0-jre</version>
</dependency>
```

```java
import com.google.common.cache.Cache;
import com.google.common.cache.CacheBuilder;

Cache<String, String> cache = CacheBuilder.newBuilder()
    .maximumSize(100)
    .expireAfterWrite(java.time.Duration.ofMinutes(10))
    .build();

cache.put("key", "value");
String val = cache.getIfPresent("key");  // no loading
```

Note: Guava caches are **not thread‑safe by default** unless you configure it that way or use `CacheBuilder.newBuilder().weakValues()`/`concurrencyLevel(...)`, but the LRU eviction is automatic.

