## 6️⃣ Why this meets your constraints

1. **Read‑your‑writes consistency across replicas:**  
   *A client’s write is only acknowledged after the log entry has been replicated and applied on a majority of nodes.* Every follower holds the same state once the commit returns, so any read from any node sees that value.

2. **No session or version metadata required:**  
   The cache stores only keys & values. Raft itself guarantees total order; clients never have to send any extra data.

3. **Simple API** – just a single PUT/GET HTTP endpoint per node.

4. **Fault‑tolerant, scalable** – add more voters and the cluster stays consistent; reads can be load‑balanced across all nodes.

