#include <stdio.h>
#include <pthread.h>

volatile int flag = 0;          /* <-- volatile only! */

void *writer(void *arg)
{
    flag = 1;
    return NULL;
}

int main()
{
    pthread_t t;
    pthread_create(&t, NULL, writer, NULL);

    while (!flag)          /* spin‑wait on a volatile read */
        ;                  /* may loop forever if compiler optimises */

    printf("Done\n");
}
```

On some systems you might see “Done” printed; on others the program can spin
forever or crash. The correct solution is to replace `volatile int flag` with
an atomic variable and use an appropriate memory order.

