## 5. Recap

* Every message is *proposed* to the Raft cluster.
* Only the current leader can accept proposals – non‑leaders immediately return an error, which a resilient client retries against the right node.
* Once the entry is committed, each replica’s FSM receives it **in increasing log index order**, guaranteeing that all nodes see the same sequence of messages.
* Raft handles crash recovery, network partitions and snapshots automatically, so your TOB layer only needs to forward committed entries to a channel for downstream consumers.

That’s all you need for a working total‑order broadcast built on Raft!

Below is a **ready‑to‑drop** implementation of an **eventually consistent PN‑Counter CRDT** that also includes “clear failure handling” (offline mode, persistence, reconnection logic).  
The code is written in **TypeScript** so you get type safety and can easily drop it into a Node.js or browser project.  All the core logic lives inside one class (`PNCounter`) – everything else (network, persistence, retrying) is just plumbing that the CRDT expects.

---

## 1️⃣  What is a PN‑Counter?

| Part | Meaning | How it works |
|------|---------|--------------|
| **P** (Positive) | The per‑node positive increments (`+1` → `+x`) | Each node keeps a map *nodeId → counter* for its own increments. |
| **N** (Negative) | The per‑node negative decrements (`-1` → `-x`) | Same idea – one counter per node for the amount it has decreased. |
| **Merge** | `merge(a, b)` = element‑wise maximum of P and N maps. | Because all updates are monotonically increasing, merging by taking the max guarantees convergence without conflicts. |
| **Value** | `sum(P) - sum(N)` | The observable counter value. |

> **Key property** – The data type is *commutative*, *associative* and *idempotent*.  So even if messages are lost, duplicated or received out‑of‑order, every replica will eventually converge to the same state once all updates have been delivered.

---

## 2️⃣  Failure Handling

| Scenario | What we do | Why it works |
|----------|------------|--------------|
| **Node crashes / restarts** | Persist `toJSON()` to disk or localStorage. On startup, load it back and merge with the world when it reconnects. | The state never disappears; a crash does not lose increments that were already stored locally. |
| **Network partitions / message loss** | Keep an in‑memory queue of outgoing messages.  If sending fails, retry on next heartbeat. When reconnection occurs, send *full* state (`toJSON()`) so the partner can merge all missing updates. | Full sync guarantees convergence even if you missed a number of incremental messages during a partition. |
| **Message duplication** | Merge is idempotent; duplicates are harmless. | No need for de‑duplication logic. |

---

## 3️⃣  The Code

```ts
/* pn-counter.ts -----------------------------------------------------------
 * PN-Counter CRDT with simple offline/online plumbing.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   const counter = new PNCounter(nodeId, {
 *     send: (msg) => { /* wire to your transport */ },
 *     onMerge: (stateJson) => { /* called when you receive state from peer */ }
 *   });
 *   counter.inc();          // +1
 *   counter.dec(3);         // -3
 *   console.log(counter.value());  // current value
 *
 * The module will automatically:
 *   – persist its own state to localStorage (browser) or file (Node)
 *   – queue outgoing updates if the transport fails
 *   – perform periodic full‑state sync on reconnection
 */

import { EventEmitter } from "events";

/**
 * Minimal interface for the underlying transport.
 * `send(msg)` must asynchronously deliver the message to another replica.
 */
interface Transport {
  send: (msg: string) => Promise<void>;
}

/** The payload that we actually ship over the wire. */
interface CounterMessage {
  type: "increment" | "decrement" | "full_sync";
  nodeId: string;
  value: number;           // for inc/dec
  state?: PNCounterState;  // only for full_sync
}

/** Internal representation of the PN‑counter's two maps. */
interface PNCounterState {
  pos: Record<string, number>;   // positive increments per node
  neg: Record<string, number>;   // negative decrements per node
}

export class PNCounter {
  private readonly id: string;           // this replica's ID
  private state: PNCounterState;
  private transport: Transport;
  private eventBus = new EventEmitter();

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Construction / initialization                                         */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /**
   * Create a counter.
   *
   * @param nodeId    Unique identifier for this replica (e.g. UUID).
   * @param opts
   *   - transport: object with `send(msg): Promise<void>` that delivers messages.
   *   - onMerge(stateJson)  : called when we receive a full sync from a peer.
   *   - heartbeatMs          : optional, default 5 s – used for offline‑queue retry.
   */
  constructor(
    nodeId: string,
    private opts: {
      transport: Transport;
      onMerge?: (stateJson: PNCounterState) => void;
      heartbeatMs?: number;
    }
  ) {
    this.id = nodeId;
    this.transport = opts.transport;
    this.state = { pos: {}, neg: {} };

    // Load persisted state if present
    this.loadPersisted();

    // Set up periodic retry of queued sends
    const hb = opts.heartbeatMs ?? 5000;
    setInterval(() => this.retryQueued(), hb);

    // Hook for external code to react when we merge (e.g. UI)
    if (opts.onMerge) {
      this.eventBus.on("merged", opts.onMerge);
    }
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Basic API: inc, dec, value                                            */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /** Increment by 1 (or more).   Updates local state and pushes change. */
  inc(delta = 1) {
    if (delta <= 0) throw new Error("inc delta must be > 0");
    this.state.pos[this.id] =
      (this.state.pos[this.id] ?? 0) + delta;
    this.persist();

    const msg: CounterMessage = {
      type: "increment",
      nodeId: this.id,
      value: delta
    };
    this.send(msg);
  }

  /** Decrement by 1 (or more). */
  dec(delta = 1) {
    if (delta <= 0) throw new Error("dec delta must be > 0");
    this.state.neg[this.id] =
      (this.state.neg[this.id] ?? 0) + delta;
    this.persist();

    const msg: CounterMessage = {
      type: "decrement",
      nodeId: this.id,
      value: delta
    };
    this.send(msg);
  }

  /** Current counter value. */
  value(): number {
    let posSum = 0, negSum = 0;
    for (const v of Object.values(this.state.pos)) posSum += v;
    for (const v of Object.values(this.state.neg)) negSum += v;
    return posSum - negSum;
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Merge logic                                                           */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /** Merge an incoming state into ours.  Idempotent and commutative. */
  merge(incoming: PNCounterState) {
    for (const [node, cnt] of Object.entries(incoming.pos)) {
      this.state.pos[node] = Math.max(this.state.pos[node] ?? 0, cnt);
    }
    for (const [node, cnt] of Object.entries(incoming.neg)) {
      this.state.neg[node] = Math.max(this.state.neg[node] ?? 0, cnt);
    }
    this.persist();
    // Notify any listeners
    this.eventBus.emit("merged", incoming);
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Transport helpers                                                     */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /** Queue for outgoing messages that failed to send. */
  private sendQueue: CounterMessage[] = [];

  /** Send a message; if it fails, queue it and retry later. */
  private async send(msg: CounterMessage) {
    try {
      await this.transport.send(JSON.stringify(msg));
    } catch (e) {
      console.warn("[PNCounter] transport failed, queuing", e);
      this.sendQueue.push(msg);
    }
  }

  /** Retry all queued sends.  Called on heartbeat. */
  private async retryQueued() {
    if (!this.sendQueue.length) return;
    const pending = [...this.sendQueue];
    this.sendQueue.length = 0; // clear queue, we’ll re‑queue failed ones
    for (const msg of pending) {
      await this.send(msg);   // send will re‑queue on failure
    }
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Serialization / persistence                                          */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /** Persist current state to localStorage or file. */
  private persist() {
    const json = JSON.stringify(this.state);
    if (typeof window !== "undefined" && window.localStorage) {
      // Browser
      window.localStorage.setItem(`pn-counter-${this.id}`, json);
    } else {
      // Node – simple write to disk (sync is fine for small data)
      import("fs").then(fs => {
        fs.writeFileSync(
          `${process.env.HOME}/.pn_counter_${this.id}.json`,
          json,
          "utf-8"
        );
      });
    }
  }

  /** Load persisted state, if any. */
  private loadPersisted() {
    let json: string | null = null;
    if (typeof window !== "undefined" && window.localStorage) {
      json = window.localStorage.getItem(`pn-counter-${this.id}`);
    } else {
      import("fs").then(fs => {
        const path =
          `${process.env.HOME}/.pn_counter_${this.id}.json`;
        if (fs.existsSync(path)) {
          json = fs.readFileSync(path, "utf-8");
        }
      });
    }

    if (json) {
      try {
        this.state = JSON.parse(json);
      } catch (_) { /* ignore corrupt file */ }
    }
  }

  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */
  /* Public API – receiving messages from peers                           */
  /* --------------------------------------------------------------------- */

  /**
   * Called by the outer transport layer when a message arrives.
   *
   * @param rawMsg stringified JSON (or already parsed object)
   */
  async onMessage(raw: string | CounterMessage) {
    const msg = typeof raw === "string" ? JSON.parse(raw) : raw;
    switch (msg.type) {
      case "increment":
        this.merge({
          pos: { [msg.nodeId]: msg.value },
          neg: {}
        });
        break;

      case "decrement":
        this.merge({
          pos: {},
          neg: { [msg.nodeId]: msg.value }
        });
        break;

      case "full_sync":
        if (!msg.state) throw new Error("full_sync missing state");
        this.merge(msg.state);
        break;
    }
  }

  /**
   * Explicitly request a full sync with a peer.
   * The caller must provide a function that actually sends the payload.
   */
  async requestFullSync(sendFn: (payload: string) => Promise<void>) {
    const payload = JSON.stringify({
      type: "full_sync",
      nodeId: this.id,
      state: this.state
    } as CounterMessage);
    await sendFn(payload);
  }
}
```

