Below is a **tiny, self‑contained program** that shows how to read an NMEA‑0183 sentence and turn it into something useful – e.g., the latitude/longitude pair that most people actually care about.  
The example uses the very popular community package  

```
github.com/adrianmo/go-nmea
```

which does all the “heavy lifting” for you (checksum, field names, type‑safe structs, etc.).  
If you prefer a pure‑Go solution you can see the small helper that parses a single sentence at the end of this post.

---

## Minimal working example – using *go-nmea*

```go
package main

import (
	"bufio"
	"fmt"
	"log"
	"os"

	nmea "github.com/adrianmo/go-nmea"
)

func main() {
	// For demo purposes we read from stdin.  
	// In a real GPS driver you would open the serial port,
	// e.g. /dev/ttyUSB0 or COM3, and feed that into the scanner.
	fmt.Println("Enter NMEA sentences (Ctrl-D to finish):")

	scanner := bufio.NewScanner(os.Stdin)

	for scanner.Scan() {
		line := scanner.Text()
		if line == "" {
			continue
		}

		pkt, err := nmea.Parse(line)
		if err != nil {
			log.Printf("❌  parse error: %v", err)
			continue
		}

		switch v := pkt.(type) {
		case *nmea.RMC:
			// RMC = Recommended Minimum Specific GPS/Transit Data
			fmt.Printf("\n=== RMC ===\n")
			fmt.Printf("Time      : %s\n", v.Time)
			fmt.Printf("Status    : %s\n", v.Status)
			fmt.Printf("Lat/Lon   : %.6f / %.6f\n",
				v.Latitude.Value(), v.Longitude.Value())
			if v.SpeedKnots.Valid() {
				fmt.Printf("Speed (kn) : %.1f\n", v.SpeedKnots.Value)
			}
			if v.Date.Valid() {
				fmt.Printf("Date       : %s\n", v.Date.String())
			}

		case *nmea.GGA:
			// GGA = Global Positioning System Fix Data
			fmt.Printf("\n=== GGA ===\n")
			fmt.Printf("Time      : %s\n", v.Time)
			fmt.Printf("Lat/Lon   : %.6f / %.6f\n",
				v.Latitude.Value(), v.Longitude.Value())
			if v.Altitude.Valid() {
				fmt.Printf("Altitude (m) : %.2f\n", v.Altitude.Value)
			}
			fmt.Printf("Satellites  : %d\n", v.SatellitesInUse)

		default:
			// If you want to see every sentence type that came in:
			fmt.Printf("\n%s\n", pkt.String())
		}
	}

	if err := scanner.Err(); err != nil {
		log.Fatalf("Scanner error: %v", err)
	}
}
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens |
|------|--------------|
| `scanner.Scan()` | Reads a whole line (an NMEA sentence). |
| `nmea.Parse(line)` | Splits the sentence, validates the checksum, and turns it into one of the exported structs (`RMC`, `GGA`, …). |
| type‑switch | We do something only for the types we care about; all other sentences are printed as raw. |

