## 5. Verify a JWT

```js
// verify.js
import { JwtEdDSATurbo } from 'jwt-ed25519-turbo';
import { publicJwk } from './key-gen.js';

const verifier = new JwtEdDSATurbo();

const token =
  'eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCIsImtpZCI6Im15LWtleS0xIn0.eyJzdWIiOiJ1c2VyLTEyMzQiLCJuYW1lIjoiQWRhIExvdmVjYWNlIiwiZXhwIjoxNzAwMjU4ODAwfQ.q5kXKp9...';

try {
  const payload = verifier.verify(token, publicJwk);
  console.log('✅ Token is valid. Payload:', payload);
} catch (err) {
  console.error('❌ Token verification failed:', err.message);
}
```

> **Common errors**  
> *`Invalid or missing token`* – The string you pass isn’t a JWT.  
> *`Signature verification failed`* – The token was signed with another key, or the header `alg` is wrong.

