## 8. Quick FAQ

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| **Can I use PEM keys?** | Yes – pass a string like `-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY----- …` to `signer.sign(..., pemKey)` and the same for verify. |
| **Do I need Node ≥ 16?** | No, because it uses WebCrypto/JavaScript only. Works in older Node (≥12) as well. |
| **What about JWT headers?** | Add custom header fields via `options.header`. The library automatically sets `"alg":"EdDSA"` when you supply an Ed25519 key. |
| **How do I protect my private key?** | Store it encrypted or in a hardware HSM (e.g., AWS KMS). Keep the JWK’s `d` field secret. |
| **Can I use this with Express?** | Yes – just plug into your route handlers; no extra dependencies beyond what you already need for JWT handling. |

