Unified Memory allows you to allocate memory that is accessible from both the host (CPU) and device (GPU) without needing to manually manage data transfers between them. The GPU runtime will automatically page memory in and out of the GPU memory space, ensuring that the data remains consistent across both devices. However, it's important to note that while Unified Memory simplifies memory management, there are still some performance considerations.

