For this example, I'll use **PicoQuic**, an open-source QUIC library written in C that provides a relatively simple API to work with QUIC. PicoQuic is part of the FastTCP project at Microsoft Research and is designed for performance and correctness.

### Step-by-Step Guide

#### 1. Install Dependencies
First, you'll need to install some dependencies if they're not already installed on your system:
```sh
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install cmake build-essential git libssl-dev
```

#### 2. Clone PicoQuic Repository
