4. **Reading and Writing**: The loop continues until the end of the source file is reached (`sourceChannel.read(buffer) != -1`). Each iteration reads from the source channel into the buffer, flips the buffer for writing, writes it to the destination channel, and then clears the buffer for reading again.

This method is efficient because it uses direct I/O operations provided by `FileChannel`, which can bypass certain layers of caching that might slow down file transfers.

