    self.values.get(&value).unwrap_or_default()
}
```
This will return `0` if the value is not found in the map, instead of panicking.

Note that this implementation assumes that the values in the PN-Counter are unique and non-negative. If there can be duplicates or negative counts, we may need to handle those cases differently.

