* The `get_and_increment_counter()` function uses a sequence of memory barriers to ensure thread-safety.
    * `lfence`: Reads the current value of the counter without interfering with any other operations.
    * Increment the counter.
    * `sfence`: Writes the updated value of the counter back to memory, making it visible to all other threads.
* No atomic operations are used, but the sequence of memory barriers guarantees thread-safety.

