The term "idempotent" means that making multiple identical requests will have the same effect as making a single request. It’s often used in HTTP methods like GET, PUT, and DELETE where their behavior is defined by the standard. 

The term "at-least-once delivery" refers to the fact that some data might be processed more than once during system failure scenarios. This can be achieved with a combination of mechanisms such as message queuing systems (like RabbitMQ, Kafka), duplicate detection, and idempotent processing.

