With this setup, every time a file is changed that has an impact on the Node.js or ExpressJS code running (e.g., changes to route handlers, modifications in middleware etc.), Nodemon will restart the server for you. 

It's important to note that Nodemon watches for any changes in your `.js` files and won’t detect changes within libraries or frameworks unless they are built-in modules (like express). For example, if a library is updated but it was not written by the developer running the server then Nodemon will not restart as there have been no code changes that affect the server logic in your application.

