Below is a **self‑contained, minimal Java example** that shows the skeleton of a consensus module built on top of a tiny, simulated asynchronous network.  
The module uses a simple **majority‑based** approach (2 out of 3 nodes) so that agreement is still reached if a single node crashes.  

> **⚠️ Disclaimer** – The FLP impossibility result tells us that *no deterministic* algorithm can guarantee consensus in a purely asynchronous network when even a single node may fail.  
> The code below is therefore **illustrative only** and is *not* a production‑grade consensus protocol (think Paxos, Raft, etc.).  It shows the idea of “collect ACKs from a majority and then broadcast a DECIDE”, together with a safety‑net that retries after a timeout.

---

## 1.  `Network` – a tiny asynchronous message bus

```java
// ---------- Network.java ----------
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;

public class Network {
    /** One inbox (queue) per node */
    private final Map<Integer, BlockingQueue<ConsensusModule.Message>> inboxes =
            new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    private final Random rnd = new Random();
    private final ExecutorService senderPool = Executors.newCachedThreadPool();

    /** Register a node so it can receive messages */
    public void register(int nodeId) {
        inboxes.put(nodeId, new LinkedBlockingQueue<>());
    }

    /** Asynchronously deliver a message after a short, random delay */
    public void send(int from, int to, ConsensusModule.Message msg) {
        senderPool.submit(() -> {
            try {
                // simulate network latency (10‑60 ms)
                Thread.sleep(rnd.nextInt(50) + 10);
                BlockingQueue<ConsensusModule.Message> inbox = inboxes.get(to);
                if (inbox != null) inbox.offer(msg);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            }
        });
    }

    /** The inbox a node uses to pull incoming messages */
    public BlockingQueue<ConsensusModule.Message> getInbox(int nodeId) {
        return inboxes.get(nodeId);
    }

    /** Clean shutdown of the simulated network */
    public void shutdown() {
        senderPool.shutdownNow();
    }
}
```

---

## 2.  `ConsensusModule` – the consensus logic

```java
// ---------- ConsensusModule.java ----------
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.*;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.*;

public class ConsensusModule implements Runnable {

    /* ---------- Message types ---------- */
    public enum MsgType { PROPOSE, ACK, DECIDE }

    public static class Message {
        public final MsgType type;
        public final int senderId;
        public final Object value;          // the proposed value

        public Message(MsgType type, int senderId, Object value) {
            this.type = type;
            this.senderId = senderId;
            this.value = value;
        }
    }

    /* ---------- Instance fields ---------- */
    private final int nodeId;
    private final Set<Integer> peers;        // IDs of the other nodes
    private final Network network;
    private final BlockingQueue<Message> inbox;

    private final ReentrantLock stateLock = new ReentrantLock();
    private final Condition decidedCond = stateLock.newCondition();

    private volatile boolean decided = false;
    private volatile Object decidedValue = null;

    /** The value this node is currently trying to get accepted */
    private volatile Object pendingProposal = null;
    /** How many ACKs we have received (including self‑ACK) for the pending proposal */
    private final AtomicInteger pendingAckCount = new AtomicInteger(0);

    /** Background timer that will retry a proposal if nothing happens for a while */
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler =
            Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);
    private volatile boolean running = true;

    /* ---------- Constructor ---------- */
    public ConsensusModule(int nodeId, Set<Integer> peers, Network network) {
        this.nodeId = nodeId;
        this.peers = peers;
        this.network = network;
        this.inbox = network.getInbox(nodeId);
    }

    /* ---------- Public API ---------- */
    public void start() {
        Thread t = new Thread(this, "ConsensusNode-" + nodeId);
        t.setDaemon(true);
        t.start();

        // If we haven’t heard a DECIDE after 10 s, try to become proposer ourselves.
        // In a real protocol you would run a leader‑election first.
        scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(() -> {
            if (!decided && pendingProposal == null) {
                try {
                    propose(nodeId);           // deterministic fallback value
                } catch (Exception ignored) { }
            }
        }, 10, 10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
    }

    /**
     * Propose a value and block until consensus is reached.
     *
     * @return the value that has been agreed upon
     * @throws Exception if the round times out (no majority)
     */
    public Object propose(Object value) throws Exception {
        stateLock.lock();
        try {
            // Reset round state
            decided = false;
            decidedValue = null;
            pendingProposal = value;
            pendingAckCount.set(1);               // self‑ACK

            // Broadcast PROPOSE to all peers
            for (int p : peers)
                network.send(nodeId, p,
                        new Message(MsgType.PROPOSE, nodeId, value));

            // Wait for a DECIDE or a 5‑second timeout
            long deadline = System.currentTimeMillis() + 5_000;
            while (!decided && System.currentTimeMillis() < deadline)
                decidedCond.await(deadline - System.currentTimeMillis(),
                        TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);

            if (!decided) {
                // Timeout → clear pending so a later round can start
                pendingProposal = null;
                throw new Exception("Consensus timed out for value: " + value);
            }
            return decidedValue;
        } finally {
            stateLock.unlock();
        }
    }

    /** Returns the decided value, blocking until it is known */
    public Object getDecision() {
        stateLock.lock();
        try {
            while (!decided) decidedCond.await();
            return decidedValue;
        } catch (InterruptedException e) {
            Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
            return null;
        } finally {
            stateLock.unlock();
        }
    }

    public void shutdown() {
        running = false;
        scheduler.shutdownNow();
    }

    /* ---------- Message handling loop ---------- */
    @Override
    public void run() {
        while (running) {
            try {
                Message msg = inbox.poll(1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
                if (msg != null) handleMessage(msg);
            } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
                break;
            }
        }
    }

    private void handleMessage(Message msg) {
        switch (msg.type) {
            case PROPOSE:
                // Always ACK a proposal (accept phase)
                network.send(nodeId, msg.senderId,
                        new Message(MsgType.ACK, nodeId, msg.value));
                // If we have not decided yet and have no own pending value,
                // remember this one – it might become our fallback.
                stateLock.lock();
                try {
                    if (!decided && pendingProposal == null) {
                        pendingProposal = msg.value;
                        pendingAckCount.set(1);
                    }
                } finally {
                    stateLock.unlock();
                }
                break;

            case ACK:
                // Count ACKs for the value we are currently proposing
                if (pendingProposal != null && Objects.equals(msg.value, pendingProposal)) {
                    int cnt = pendingAckCount.incrementAndGet();
                    if (cnt >= majority() && !decided) {
                        decide(msg.value);
                        // Broadcast DECIDE so everybody commits
                        for (int p : peers)
                            network.send(nodeId, p,
                                    new Message(MsgType.DECIDE, nodeId, msg.value));
                    }
                }
                break;

            case DECIDE:
                decide(msg.value);
                break;
        }
    }

    /* ---------- Helpers ---------- */
    /** Majority needed to commit – for 3 nodes, 2 is enough */
    private int majority() {
        return peers.size() / 2 + 1;
    }

    private void decide(Object value) {
        stateLock.lock();
        try {
            if (!decided) {
                decided = true;
                decidedValue = value;
                pendingProposal = null;   // clear any pending round
                decidedCond.signalAll();
            }
        } finally {
            stateLock.unlock();
        }
    }
}
```

