| **Digital signatures** | Any IND‑CMA‑secure scheme (RSA‑PSS, Ed25519, ECDSA, BLS). In the code below we mock a HMAC‑based scheme for illustration. |
| **Threshold (aggregate) signatures** | In a production system you would use a **threshold BLS** or **threshold Schnorr** library (e.g. `bls-signatures`, `KZenNetworks/threshold-signatures`). The code shows how to treat a set of ordinary signatures as a “threshold signature’’ (just verify each and count). |
| **Common coin / randomness** | The toy protocol is **synchronous** – we assume that all messages are eventually delivered. If you need liveness in a partially synchronous setting you add a “locked‑value’’ mechanism (like PBFT/HotStuff) and a cryptographic **common coin** to break ties. |
| **Network model** | Partial synchrony (the typical assumption for BFT). We simulate a reliable broadcast channel with a central `Network` object that delivers messages to all nodes. |

