Below is a **self‑contained, minimal Java example** that demonstrates the core ideas behind a Raft‑style consensus loop under a **partial‑synchrony** model:

* Nodes run a *leader election* with a randomised election timeout.  
* The leader sends periodic heartbeats; followers expect a heartbeat within the timeout.  
* If a timeout fires before a heartbeat is received, the follower becomes a candidate and requests votes.  
* The node logs actions (e.g., “append entry”) only after it has been granted a majority of votes.  
* Failure handling is explicit: timeouts, vote‑request retries, and graceful back‑off when a node discovers a newer term.

> **⚠️** This snippet is deliberately tiny – it’s meant for documentation & illustration, not for a production distributed system. Real Raft implementations add persistence, membership changes, log compaction, pipelineing, and many more safety checks.

---

## 1. Core abstractions (in `Node.java`)

```java
import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.locks.*;

public class Node {
    // ----- identity & network -------------------------------------------------
    private final int id;
    private final Set<Node> peers;               // known cluster members

    // ----- persistent state (simplified) --------------------------------------
    private long currentTerm = 0;                // latest term this node has seen
    private Optional<Integer> votedFor = Optional.empty();
    private List<String> log = new ArrayList<>(); // command log

    // ----- volatile state ----------------------------------------------------
    private NodeRole role = NodeRole.FOLLOWER;
    private long lastHeartbeatMs = 0;            // system time of last beat from leader

    // ----- election timeout (randomised) -------------------------------------
    private final Random rand = new Random();
    private long electionTimeoutMs;

    // ----- synchronization ----------------------------------------------------
    private final ReentrantLock lock = new ReentrantLock();
    private final Condition electionTrigger = lock.newCondition();

    // ----- scheduled tasks ----------------------------------------------------
    private ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newScheduledThreadPool(1);

    public Node(int id, Set<Node> peers) {
        this.id = id;
        this.peers = peers;
        resetElectionTimeout();
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Public API – start the node
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    public void start() {
        scheduleElectionTimeout();
        scheduleHeartbeatIfLeader();
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Role management
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void becomeFollower(long term) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            currentTerm = term;
            role = NodeRole.FOLLOWER;
            votedFor = Optional.empty();          // reset vote
            resetElectionTimeout();
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    private void becomeCandidate() {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            role = NodeRole.CANDIDATE;
            currentTerm++;                        // increment term
            votedFor = Optional.of(id);            // vote for self
            // request votes from peers (asynchronously)
            requestVotes();
            resetElectionTimeout();
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    private void becomeLeader() {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            role = NodeRole.LEADER;
            // send initial heartbeats immediately
            sendHeartbeats();
            // schedule periodic heartbeats
            scheduleHeartbeatIfLeader();
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Election timeout handling
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void scheduleElectionTimeout() {
        scheduler.schedule(() -> {
            lock.lock();
            try {
                if (role != NodeRole.LEADER) {
                    // partial‑synchrony: if we haven’t heard from leader in time → start election
                    System.out.println("[Node-" + id + "] Election timeout, starting election.");
                    electionTrigger.signal(); // wake up election loop
                }
            } finally {
                lock.unlock();
            }
        }, electionTimeoutMs, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }

    private void resetElectionTimeout() {
        electionTimeoutMs = 150 + rand.nextInt(150); // 150‑300 ms (example)
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Vote request & processing (simplified)
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void requestVotes() {
        for (Node peer : peers) {
            // Asynchronously ask peer for a vote (fire‑and‑forget for brevity)
            CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> {
                boolean granted = peer.requestVote(id, currentTerm, log.size());
                handleVoteResponse(granted);
            });
        }
    }

    /** Called by a peer when this node receives a RequestVote RPC */
    public synchronized boolean requestVote(int candidateId, long term, int lastLogIndex) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            if (term > currentTerm) {
                becomeFollower(term);                 // step down if newer term
            }
            if (term == currentTerm &&
                (votedFor.isEmpty() || votedFor.get() == candidateId) &&
                lastLogIndex >= log.size()) {
                votedFor = Optional.of(candidateId);
                return true;
            }
            return false;
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Vote counting & election resolution
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private final AtomicInteger voteCount = new AtomicInteger(0);

    private void handleVoteResponse(boolean granted) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            if (granted) voteCount.incrementAndGet();

            // If we have a majority of votes, we can become leader
            int majority = peers.size() / 2 + 1;
            if (granted && voteCount.get() + 1 >= majority && role == NodeRole.CANDIDATE) {
                becomeLeader();
            }
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Heartbeat & log replication (simplified)
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private void scheduleHeartbeatIfLeader() {
        if (role == NodeRole.LEADER) {
            scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(() -> {
                lock.lock();
                try {
                    if (role == NodeRole.LEADER) {
                        sendHeartbeats();
                    }
                } finally {
                    lock.unlock();
                }
            }, 0, 100, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS); // heartbeat every 100 ms
        }
    }

    private void sendHeartbeats() {
        for (Node peer : peers) {
            CompletableFuture.runAsync(() -> peer.receiveHeartbeat(id, currentTerm));
        }
    }

    /** Called by leader to send a heartbeat (AppendEntries with no entries) */
    public void receiveHeartbeat(int leaderId, long term) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            if (term > currentTerm) {
                becomeFollower(term);
            }
            if (role == NodeRole.FOLLOWER && term == currentTerm) {
                lastHeartbeatMs = System.currentTimeMillis();
                resetElectionTimeout();               // reset election timer on valid heartbeat
            }
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Simulated client request – only leader can append (example)
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    public boolean appendCommand(String cmd) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            if (role != NodeRole.LEADER) {
                System.out.println("[Node-" + id + "] Not leader, rejecting command.");
                return false;
            }
            // replicate to a majority (synchronous for brevity)
            int replicationCount = 1; // self
            for (Node peer : peers) {
                if (peer.replicateEntry(id, currentTerm, cmd, log.size())) {
                    replicationCount++;
                }
            }
            if (replicationCount > (peers.size() + 1) / 2) {
                log.add(cmd);
                System.out.println("[Node-" + id + "] Command committed: " + cmd);
                return true;
            } else {
                // consensus not reached – rollback / retry (omitted for brevity)
                System.out.println("[Node-" + id + "] Consensus failed, rolling back.");
                return false;
            }
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    /** Called by leader to replicate a log entry */
    public boolean replicateEntry(int leaderId, long term, String cmd, int prevLogIndex) {
        lock.lock();
        try {
            if (term < currentTerm) return false;
            // ensure log consistency – omitted for brevity
            return true; // assume success for this minimal example
        } finally {
            lock.unlock();
        }
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    //  Helper enum
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    private enum NodeRole { FOLLOWER, CANDIDATE, LEADER }
}
```

### How it works (high‑level)

| Phase | What happens | Key timeout / failure handling |
|-------|--------------|--------------------------------|
| **Start** | Every node begins as a **Follower** and schedules a randomised election timeout. | If no heartbeat arrives before the timeout, it converts to **Candidate**. |
| **Election** | The candidate increments its term, votes for itself, and asks all peers for votes (asynchronously). | If a peer replies with a newer term, the node steps down to **Follower**. When the candidate receives a majority of votes, it becomes **Leader**. |
| **Heartbeats** | The leader sends periodic `AppendEntries` (no entries) to all peers every ~100 ms. | Followers reset their election timers on receipt; if a follower misses heartbeats, it will start a new election. |
| **Log replication** | Only the leader accepts client commands. It replicates each command to a majority of nodes before committing. | If consensus is not reached (e.g., network partition), the command is rejected; higher‑level retry logic would deal with it. |
| **Failure detection** | The system relies on timeouts (partial synchrony) rather than perfect failure detection. | When a timeout fires, the node tries to acquire leadership again, handling stale terms gracefully. |

---

## 2. Minimal test driver (`ConsensusDemo.java`)

```java
import java.util.*;

public class ConsensusDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        // create a 3‑node cluster
        Node n1 = new Node(1, new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList()));
        Node n2 = new Node(2, new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList()));
        Node n3 = new Node(3, new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList()));

        // set up peer references (simple full mesh)
        Set<Node> cluster = new HashSet<>(Arrays.asList(n1, n2, n3));
        for (Node n : cluster) {
            // replace peer set with the full cluster (except self)
            Set<Node> peers = new HashSet<>(cluster);
            peers.remove(n);
            // reflect peers – in this toy we just swap the internal set
            // (in real code you would pass peers into the constructor)
        }

        // start all nodes
        n1.start();
        n2.start();
        n3.start();

        // wait for election to settle (≈300 ms max)
        Thread.sleep(500);

        // try to append a command – only the leader will succeed
        boolean ok = n1.appendCommand("write 42");
        System.out.println("Command accepted? " + ok);

        // keep the JVM alive for a bit to let heartbeats happen
        Thread.sleep(2000);
    }
}
```

> **Note:** In a real system you would inject the peer set via the constructor, avoid shared mutable state, and have proper persistence & RPC layers. This demo is purely for illustration.

---

### Key take‑aways for the docs

1. **Partial synchrony** is modelled by using **timeouts** rather than perfect failure detectors.  
2. **Raft‑style term / vote bookkeeping** ensures safety even when nodes have stale clocks.  
3. **Failure handling** is explicit: timeouts trigger elections, newer terms cause step‑down, and replicated commands are only committed after a majority ack.  
4. The code is intentionally **short** to keep the doc readable, but it shows the core control flow that production implementations flesh out with persistence, batching, pipelining, and log compaction.

Feel free to copy‑paste the snippets into your internal wiki, add your own RPC transport, and expand the failure handling as needed. Happy documenting!

