| **Range** | A 64‑bit counter can exceed 4 × 10⁹ (the limit of a 32‑bit `int`), which is useful for long‑running services that may see billions of requests. |
| **Performance** | Using `memory_order_relaxed` (when ordering constraints aren’t needed) eliminates unnecessary memory barriers, keeping the hot path as fast as possible. |

