// and in the loop:
else if (c == '«') { stack.push(c); }
```

The rest of the algorithm stays exactly the same!

---

## 7️⃣  Take‑away

- Use a **stack** (`Deque`/`ArrayDeque`) to keep track of unmatched opening brackets.  
- A **hash map** (or a simple `switch`) maps each closing bracket to its opening counterpart.  
- Adding a fourth pair (`<` / `>`) is a one‑line change in the map and one extra condition in the `else if` block.

