| **Wireless interface is up** | `ip link set wlan0 up` (but `wpa_supplicant` usually does this for you). |
| **Correct driver** | Make sure the NIC driver supports `nl80211` (most modern drivers do). |
| **Certificates (if needed)** | Have the CA/ client certs in a place readable by the process, and pass the paths via `ca_cert`, `client_cert`, `private_key` commands. |
| **No conflicting network manager** | Disable or pause `NetworkManager` (`systemctl stop NetworkManager`) while you experiment, otherwise it may try to manage the interface simultaneously. |
