| Step | Explanation |
|------|-------------|
| **Include** | `<experimental/simd_sort>` brings the function template `std::experimental::simd_sort` into scope. |
| **Data generation** | `std::vector<float> data(N)` holds the numbers. We fill it with random `float`s so we have something to sort. |
| **Call the sort** | `std::experimental::simd_sort(data.begin(), data.end())` rearranges the elements in **ascending** order using SIMD instructions internally. |
| **Comparator (optional)** | If you need descending order you can supply a comparator, e.g.: <br>`std::experimental::simd_sort(data.begin(), data.end(), std::greater<float>{});` |
| **Timing & verification** | The example measures how long the sort takes and checks `std::is_sorted` to prove correctness. |
| **Output** | Prints a quick sanity check (first/last few values). |

