## 4. If your standard library *doesn’t* ship `<experimental/simd_sort>`

The experimental header is **not** part of any ISO C++ standard yet, so some distributions may not have it. You can fall back to a standalone implementation that follows the same API:

* **GitHub – Intel simd‑sort** (header‑only): <https://github.com/intel/simd-sort>  

  The repository contains a file called `simd_sort.h`. You can drop it into your project, rename it to `<experimental/simd_sort>` (or just keep it as `simd_sort.h` and adjust the `#include` line). The interface is deliberately compatible with the experimental proposal, e.g.:

  ```cpp
