## 3. Target Language – A Tiny Stack Machine

The stack machine has three instruction types:

| Opcode | Meaning |
|--------|---------|
| `PUSH n` | push integer constant `n` |
| `LOAD x` | push the current value of variable `x` |
| `STORE x`| pop the top of the stack and store it into `x` |
| `ADD`   | pop two ints, push their sum |
| `SUB`   | pop two ints, push left‑minus‑right |
| `MUL`   | pop two ints, push their product |
| `EQ`, `LT`, `AND`, `NOT` | analogous Boolean ops (result is 0/1) |
| `JMP L` | unconditional jump to label `L` |
| `JZ L`  | pop a value; if it is 0 jump to `L` (used for `if`/`while`) |
| `LABEL L`| a no‑op that marks a program counter location |

The **machine state** is a pair `(stack, store)`.  Execution is *small‑step*: each instruction transforms the state.

### 3.1 Bytecode data structures (Java)

```java
import java.util.*;

public final class StackVM {

    /* ----- Instructions ----- */
    sealed interface Instr permits Push, Load, Store, BinOp, UnOp, Jump, JumpZero, Label {}
    record Push(int n) implements Instr {}
    record Load(String x) implements Instr {}
    record Store(String x) implements Instr {}
    enum BinOp implements Instr { ADD, SUB, MUL, EQ, LT, AND }
    enum UnOp implements Instr { NOT }
    record Jump(String label) implements Instr {}
    record JumpZero(String label) implements Instr {}
    record Label(String name) implements Instr {}

    /* ----- Program (list of instructions) ----- */
    public static final class Program extends ArrayList<Instr> {}

    /* ----- Machine state ----- */
    public static final class State {
        Deque<Integer> stack = new ArrayDeque<>();
        Map<String,Integer> store = new HashMap<>();
        int pc = 0;               // program counter (index into Program)
        final Program prog;

        State(Program prog) { this.prog = prog; }
    }

    /* ----- Small‑step interpreter ----- */
    public static boolean step(State st) {
        if (st.pc >= st.prog.size()) return false; // halted
        Instr i = st.prog.get(st.pc);
        st.pc++; // default: advance to next instruction

        switch (i) {
            case Push p -> st.stack.push(p.n());
            case Load l -> st.stack.push(st.store.getOrDefault(l.x(), 0));
            case Store s -> {
                int v = st.stack.pop();
                st.store.put(s.x(), v);
            }
            case BinOp op -> {
                int r = st.stack.pop();
                int l = st.stack.pop();
                int res = switch (op) {
                    case ADD -> l + r;
                    case SUB -> l - r;
                    case MUL -> l * r;
                    case EQ  -> (l == r) ? 1 : 0;
                    case LT  -> (l <  r) ? 1 : 0;
                    case AND -> ((l != 0) && (r != 0)) ? 1 : 0;
                };
                st.stack.push(res);
            }
            case UnOp NOT -> {
                int v = st.stack.pop();
                st.stack.push(v == 0 ? 1 : 0);
            }
            case Jump j -> st.pc = findLabel(st.prog, j.label());
            case JumpZero jz -> {
                int v = st.stack.pop();
                if (v == 0) st.pc = findLabel(st.prog, jz.label());
            }
            case Label _ -> { /* no‑op */ }
        }
        return true;
    }

    private static int findLabel(Program prog, String name) {
        for (int i = 0; i < prog.size(); i++) {
            Instr ins = prog.get(i);
            if (ins instanceof Label l && l.name().equals(name)) return i;
        }
        throw new IllegalArgumentException("label not found: " + name);
    }

    /** Run to completion and return the final store. */
    public static Map<String,Integer> run(Program prog) {
        State s = new State(prog);
        while (step(s)) { /* loop */ }
        return s.store;
    }
}
```

