Below is a **self‑contained, runnable** Java sketch that demonstrates the core of a Raft‑style consensus algorithm under the **partial‑synchrony** model.  
It focuses on the three classic Raft responsibilities:

1. **Leader election** – driven by randomized election time‑outs.  
2. **Log replication (heartbeat)** – a periodic `AppendEntries` RPC that also serves as a liveness check.  
3. **Failure handling** – what a node does when it cannot reach a majority, when a leader disappears, or when RPCs fail.

The code is deliberately short (≈ 200 LOC) but each block is heavily commented so you can copy‑paste it into your internal documentation and expand it later.

---

## 1.  High‑level design

| Component | Responsibility |
|-----------|-----------------|
| `RaftNode` | One Raft server (follower / candidate / leader). Holds term, vote, log, timers, and the state‑machine that reacts to incoming RPCs. |
| `RaftNetwork` | Very small abstraction that delivers RPCs between nodes. In a real system this would be gRPC / Netty / HTTP, but here it is a simple in‑process dispatcher that can simulate message loss / delays. |
| `Main` | Starts a configurable cluster, lets it run for a few seconds, then shuts everything down. |

All time‑outs are **real‑time** (`ScheduledExecutorService`). Under the **partial‑synchrony** assumption the network may be arbitrarily slow or drop messages, but *eventually* messages are delivered within a bounded delay. The algorithm therefore works as long as the election timeout is **larger** than the worst‑case network delay that can be observed.

---

## 2.  The code

```java
/**
 * Minimal Raft implementation that demonstrates:
 *   • Randomised election time‑outs (partial‑synchrony)
 *   • Heartbeat / log replication (AppendEntries)
 *   • Clear failure handling (re‑election, RPC retries)
 *
 * This is **not** production‑ready – it omits persistence,
 * log compaction, membership changes, etc.  It is however
 * a complete, compile‑and‑run example.
 */
package com.example.raft;

import java.util.*;
import java.util.concurrent.*;
import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;

/* -------------------------------------------------------------
 * 1️⃣  RPC messages (very small – just enough for the demo)
 * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
record RequestVote(int term, int candidateId, int lastLogIndex, int lastLogTerm) {}
record RequestVoteResponse(int term, boolean voteGranted) {}

record AppendEntries(int term,
                     int leaderId,
                     int prevLogIndex,
                     int prevLogTerm,
                     List<LogEntry> entries,
                     int leaderCommit) {}
record AppendEntriesResponse(int term, boolean success) {}

record LogEntry(int term, String command) {}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------
 * 2️⃣  Network abstraction – in‑process, but can be swapped out.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
interface RaftNetwork {
    /** Asynchronously deliver a RequestVote RPC. */
    CompletableFuture<RequestVoteResponse> sendRequestVote(int targetId,
                                                            RequestVote rpc);

    /** Asynchronously deliver an AppendEntries RPC. */
    CompletableFuture<AppendEntriesResponse> sendAppendEntries(int targetId,
                                                                AppendEntries rpc);
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------
 * 3️⃣  The Raft node.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
class RaftNode {
    /** Raft states – exactly the three defined by the paper. */
    enum State { FOLLOWER, CANDIDATE, LEADER }

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Persistent state (would be on disk in a real implementation)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private final int id;                     // unique node identifier
    private int currentTerm = 0;
    private Integer votedFor = null;          // null = not voted yet
    private final List<LogEntry> log = new ArrayList<>();

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Volatile state
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private State state = State.FOLLOWER;
    private int commitIndex = 0;
    private int lastApplied = 0;

    // Leader‑only volatile state
    private final Map<Integer, Integer> nextIndex = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final Map<Integer, Integer> matchIndex = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Cluster view & networking
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private final List<Integer> peerIds;      // all node ids (including self)
    private final RaftNetwork network;

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Timers (scheduled on a single‑threaded executor per node)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private final ScheduledExecutorService scheduler = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
    private ScheduledFuture<?> electionTimeoutTask;
    private ScheduledFuture<?> heartbeatTask;

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Randomised election timeout (partial‑synchrony)
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    private static final int ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MIN_MS = 150;
    private static final int ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MAX_MS = 300;
    private static final int HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS   = 50;

    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    // Construction
    // -----------------------------------------------------------------
    RaftNode(int id, List<Integer> peerIds, RaftNetwork network) {
        this.id = id;
        this.peerIds = new ArrayList<>(peerIds);
        this.network = network;
        resetElectionTimeout();   // start as follower
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Public API – called by the network dispatcher
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    CompletableFuture<RequestVoteResponse> onRequestVote(RequestVote rpc) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> handleRequestVote(rpc));
    }

    CompletableFuture<AppendEntriesResponse> onAppendEntries(AppendEntries rpc) {
        return CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> handleAppendEntries(rpc));
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Core Raft logic
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private synchronized RequestVoteResponse handleRequestVote(RequestVote rpc) {
        // 1. Reply false if term < currentTerm
        if (rpc.term() < currentTerm) {
            return new RequestVoteResponse(currentTerm, false);
        }

        // 2. If term > currentTerm, step down
        if (rpc.term() > currentTerm) {
            becomeFollower(rpc.term());
        }

        // 3. Determine if we can grant the vote
        boolean voteGranted = false;
        boolean notVotedYet = (votedFor == null || votedFor == rpc.candidateId());
        boolean candidateUpToDate = isCandidateLogUpToDate(rpc.lastLogIndex(), rpc.lastLogTerm());

        if (notVotedYet && candidateUpToDate) {
            votedFor = rpc.candidateId();
            voteGranted = true;
            resetElectionTimeout(); // grant = activity, so reset timer
        }

        return new RequestVoteResponse(currentTerm, voteGranted);
    }

    private synchronized AppendEntriesResponse handleAppendEntries(AppendEntries rpc) {
        // 1. Reply false if term < currentTerm
        if (rpc.term() < currentTerm) {
            return new AppendEntriesResponse(currentTerm, false);
        }

        // 2. If term > currentTerm, step down (maybe we were candidate)
        if (rpc.term() > currentTerm) {
            becomeFollower(rpc.term());
        }

        // 3. We have a valid leader – reset election timer
        resetElectionTimeout();

        // 4. Log consistency check (simplified – we only store term)
        if (rpc.prevLogIndex() > 0) {
            if (log.size() < rpc.prevLogIndex()
                || log.get(rpc.prevLogIndex() - 1).term() != rpc.prevLogTerm()) {
                return new AppendEntriesResponse(currentTerm, false);
            }
        }

        // 5. Append any new entries (no conflict handling for brevity)
        int index = rpc.prevLogIndex();
        for (LogEntry e : rpc.entries()) {
            index++;
            if (log.size() >= index) {
                // overwrite conflicting entry
                log.set(index - 1, e);
            } else {
                log.add(e);
            }
        }

        // 6. Advance commitIndex
        if (rpc.leaderCommit() > commitIndex) {
            commitIndex = Math.min(rpc.leaderCommit(), log.size());
            // In a real system we would now apply entries to the state machine.
        }

        return new AppendEntriesResponse(currentTerm, true);
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Helper: is the candidate's log at least as up‑to‑date as ours?
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private boolean isCandidateLogUpToDate(int candidateLastIdx, int candidateLastTerm) {
        int lastTerm = (log.isEmpty()) ? 0 : log.get(log.size() - 1).term();
        int lastIdx  = log.size();
        return (candidateLastTerm > lastTerm) ||
               (candidateLastTerm == lastTerm && candidateLastIdx >= lastIdx);
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  State transitions
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private synchronized void becomeFollower(int term) {
        state = State.FOLLOWER;
        currentTerm = term;
        votedFor = null;
        cancelHeartbeat();
        resetElectionTimeout();
    }

    private synchronized void becomeCandidate() {
        state = State.CANDIDATE;
        currentTerm++;
        votedFor = id; // vote for self
        int lastLogIdx = log.size();
        int lastLogTerm = (log.isEmpty()) ? 0 : log.get(lastLogIdx - 1).term();

        // Send RequestVote RPCs in parallel
        List<CompletableFuture<RequestVoteResponse>> futures = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int peer : peerIds) {
            if (peer == id) continue;
            RequestVote rpc = new RequestVote(currentTerm, id, lastLogIdx, lastLogTerm);
            futures.add(network.sendRequestVote(peer, rpc));
        }

        // Collect votes (with a timeout to avoid waiting forever)
        CompletableFuture<Void> all = CompletableFuture.allOf(futures.toArray(new CompletableFuture[0]));
        all.orTimeout(ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MAX_MS, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS)
           .whenComplete((v, ex) -> {
               if (ex != null) {
                   // Timeout or network failure → start a new election
                   startElection();
                   return;
               }
               long granted = futures.stream()
                       .filter(f -> {
                           try { return f.get().voteGranted(); }
                           catch (Exception e) { return false; }
                       })
                       .count();

               // +1 for our own vote
               if (granted + 1 > peerIds.size() / 2) {
                   becomeLeader();
               } else {
                   // Not enough votes – wait a random back‑off then retry
                   scheduler.schedule(this::startElection,
                           randomElectionTimeout(), TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
               }
           });
    }

    private synchronized void becomeLeader() {
        state = State.LEADER;
        // Initialise leader‑only volatile state
        for (int peer : peerIds) {
            if (peer == id) continue;
            nextIndex.put(peer, log.size() + 1);
            matchIndex.put(peer, 0);
        }
        cancelElectionTimeout();
        startHeartbeats();
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Timers
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void resetElectionTimeout() {
        cancelElectionTimeout();
        long timeout = randomElectionTimeout();
        electionTimeoutTask = scheduler.schedule(this::startElection,
                timeout, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }

    private void cancelElectionTimeout() {
        if (electionTimeoutTask != null) electionTimeoutTask.cancel(false);
    }

    private void startElection() {
        if (state == State.LEADER) return; // should never happen
        becomeCandidate();
    }

    private void startHeartbeats() {
        heartbeatTask = scheduler.scheduleAtFixedRate(this::sendHeartbeats,
                0, HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_MS, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
    }

    private void cancelHeartbeat() {
        if (heartbeatTask != null) heartbeatTask.cancel(false);
    }

    private long randomElectionTimeout() {
        return ThreadLocalRandom.current()
                .nextLong(ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MIN_MS, ELECTION_TIMEOUT_MAX_MS + 1);
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Leader: send AppendEntries (heartbeat) to all followers
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    private void sendHeartbeats() {
        if (state != State.LEADER) return;

        for (int peer : peerIds) {
            if (peer == id) continue;

            int nextIdx = nextIndex.getOrDefault(peer, 1);
            int prevIdx = nextIdx - 1;
            int prevTerm = (prevIdx == 0) ? 0 : log.get(prevIdx - 1).term();

            // In this demo we never have real client commands, so entries = empty
            AppendEntries rpc = new AppendEntries(
                    currentTerm,
                    id,
                    prevIdx,
                    prevTerm,
                    Collections.emptyList(),
                    commitIndex);

            // Fire‑and‑forget – failures are handled by the follower's election timeout
            network.sendAppendEntries(peer, rpc)
                   .whenComplete((resp, ex) -> {
                       if (ex != null) {
                           // RPC failed (network partition, node down).  No immediate action.
                           return;
                       }
                       if (!resp.success()) {
                           // Leader's log is out of sync – step back nextIndex and retry later
                           nextIndex.compute(peer, (k, v) -> Math.max(1, v - 1));
                       } else {
                           // Successful heartbeat – advance nextIndex
                           nextIndex.put(peer, log.size() + 1);
                           matchIndex.put(peer, log.size());
                       }
                   });
        }
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Graceful shutdown (used by the demo Main)
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    void shutdown() {
        cancelElectionTimeout();
        cancelHeartbeat();
        scheduler.shutdownNow();
    }

    /* -------------------------------------------------------------
     *  Debug helpers
     * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
    @Override public String toString() {
        return "Node#" + id + " [" + state + "] term=" + currentTerm;
    }
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------
 * 4️⃣  In‑process network implementation (simulates loss & delay)
 * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
class InProcessNetwork implements RaftNetwork {
    private final Map<Integer, RaftNode> nodes = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    private final Random rng = new Random();

    /** Register a node so that others can address it. */
    void register(RaftNode node, int id) {
        nodes.put(id, node);
    }

    /** Simulate async RPC with optional delay / drop. */
    private <T> CompletableFuture<T> asyncCall(Callable<T> work) {
        CompletableFuture<T> cf = new CompletableFuture<>();
        // Random delay 0‑30 ms, 5 % chance of total loss
        int delay = rng.nextInt(30);
        boolean drop = rng.nextDouble() < 0.05;
        ScheduledExecutorService exec = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
        exec.schedule(() -> {
            if (drop) {
                cf.completeExceptionally(new RuntimeException("simulated network loss"));
            } else {
                try { cf.complete(work.call()); }
                catch (Exception e) { cf.completeExceptionally(e); }
            }
            exec.shutdown();
        }, delay, TimeUnit.MILLISECONDS);
        return cf;
    }

    @Override
    public CompletableFuture<RequestVoteResponse> sendRequestVote(int targetId, RequestVote rpc) {
        RaftNode target = nodes.get(targetId);
        if (target == null) return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(
                new IllegalArgumentException("unknown target " + targetId));
        return asyncCall(() -> target.onRequestVote(rpc).join());
    }

    @Override
    public CompletableFuture<AppendEntriesResponse> sendAppendEntries(int targetId, AppendEntries rpc) {
        RaftNode target = nodes.get(targetId);
        if (target == null) return CompletableFuture.failedFuture(
                new IllegalArgumentException("unknown target " + targetId));
        return asyncCall(() -> target.onAppendEntries(rpc).join());
    }
}

/* -------------------------------------------------------------
 * 5️⃣  Demo driver – spins up a 5‑node cluster and watches it.
 * ------------------------------------------------------------- */
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        final int NODE_COUNT = 5;
        InProcessNetwork net = new InProcessNetwork();

        // Build node list (ids 1..N)
        List<Integer> ids = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int i = 1; i <= NODE_COUNT; i++) ids.add(i);

        // Create and register nodes
        List<RaftNode> nodes = new ArrayList<>();
        for (int id : ids) {
            RaftNode node = new RaftNode(id, ids, net);
            net.register(node, id);
            nodes.add(node);
        }

        // Let the cluster run for a while
        System.out.println("=== Raft cluster started ===");
        ScheduledExecutorService printer = Executors.newSingleThreadScheduledExecutor();
        printer.scheduleAtFixedRate(() -> {
            System.out.println("--- Cluster view ---");
            nodes.forEach(n -> System.out.println(n));
        }, 0, 1, TimeUnit.SECONDS);

        // Run for 15 seconds then shut down
        Thread.sleep(15000);
        printer.shutdownNow();
        nodes.forEach(RaftNode::shutdown);
        System.out.println("=== Cluster stopped ===");
    }
}
```

