## 6.  Complexity recap

| Operation | Average case | Worst case |
|-----------|--------------|------------|
| **Build (static, median split)** | **O(N log N)** (due to `nth_element` at each level) | **O(N log N)** (still, because `nth_element` is linear on average) |
| **Nearest‑neighbour query** | **O(log N)** (tree is balanced) | **O(N)** (if the tree is completely unbalanced or points are pathological) |
| **Insert (dynamic)** | **O(log N)** (balanced) | **O(N)** (if tree becomes a chain) |
| **Memory** | One node per point → **O(N)** | — |

