## 4️⃣ Verify the JWT (optional but recommended)

```js
// file: verify-jwt.mjs
import { jwtVerify } from 'jose';
import { loadEd25519KeyPair } from './load-key.mjs'; // or reuse the generated key

(async () => {
  // 1️⃣ Load the public key that corresponds to the private key used for signing
  const { publicKey } = await loadEd25519KeyPair(); // replace with your own source

  // 2️⃣ The JWT we want to verify – copy it from the output of sign-jwt.mjs
  const token = 'eyJhbGciOiJFZERTQSIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...'; // <-- replace

  try {
    const { payload, protectedHeader } = await jwtVerify(token, publicKey, {
      // Optional: enforce expected claims
      issuer: 'my-awesome-app',
      audience: 'my-awesome-app-client',
    });

    console.log('✅ JWT is valid! 🎉');
    console.log('Header:', protectedHeader);
    console.log('Payload:', payload);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('❌ JWT verification failed:', err);
  }
})();
```

If the token is tampered with, expired, or signed with a different key, `jwtVerify` will throw an error.

