```

> **Why `github.com/adrianmo/go-nmea`?**  
> It implements the full NMEA‑0183 spec (checksum validation, all standard sentence types, conversion to decimal degrees, etc.) and is only ~200 KB of source. It’s battle‑tested in many hobby‑ and production‑grade projects.

> **Why `github.com/tarm/serial`?**  
> It’s the de‑facto standard Go serial‑port library. If you already have NMEA data in a file or a string you can skip this import.

