## 7. Going from “print” to “use”

Once you have a `nmea.GGA` or `nmea.RMC` struct you can:

```go
// Example: store the latest fix in a struct that can be shared safely
type Fix struct {
    mu        sync.RWMutex
    Time      time.Time
    Lat, Lon  float64 // decimal degrees
    Altitude  float64 // meters
    Valid     bool
}

func (f *Fix) UpdateFromGGA(gga nmea.GGA) {
    f.mu.Lock()
    defer f.mu.Unlock()
    f.Time = time.Date(
        time.Now().Year(), time.Now().Month(), time.Now().Day(),
        gga.Time.Hour, gga.Time.Minute, int(gga.Time.Second), 0, time.UTC)
    f.Lat = float64(gga.Latitude)
    if gga.LatitudeDirection == nmea.South {
        f.Lat = -f.Lat
    }
    f.Lon = float64(gga.Longitude)
    if gga.LongitudeDirection == nmea.West {
        f.Lon = -f.Lon
    }
    f.Altitude = gga.Altitude
    f.Valid = gga.FixQuality > 0
}
```

You can then expose `Fix` via an HTTP endpoint, push it to a message queue, write it to a database, etc. The parsing code stays exactly the same.

