## 3. Windows – PCAN‑Basic (PEAK‑Systems)

If you are on Windows you’ll most likely use the **PCAN‑Basic** SDK (free for non‑commercial use). The API is C‑style but works fine from C++.

### 3.1. Install the SDK

1. Download the latest *PCAN‑Basic* package from <https://www.peak-system.com/PCAN-Basic.239.0.html>.
2. Run the installer – it puts `PCANBasic.h` and `PCANBasic.lib` in `C:\Program Files\PEAK-System\PCAN-Basic`.

### 3.2. Minimal program

```cpp
// read_pcan.cpp ------------------------------------------------------------
#include <iostream>
#include <iomanip>
#include "PCANBasic.h"

int main()
{
    // 1️⃣ Open channel 0 (PCAN-USB) at 500 kbps
    TPCANStatus status = CAN_Initialize(PCAN_USBBUS1, PCAN_BAUD_500K);
    if (status != PCAN_ERROR_OK) {
        char err[256];
        CAN_GetErrorText(status, 0x09, err);
        std::cerr << "CAN_Initialize failed: " << err << '\n';
        return 1;
    }

    std::cout << "PCAN-USB channel opened, listening …\n";

    // 2️⃣ Receive loop
    while (true) {
        TPCANMsg msg{};
        TPCANTimestamp ts{};
        status = CAN_Read(PCAN_USBBUS1, &msg, &ts);
        if (status == PCAN_ERROR_OK) {
            std::cout << std::hex << std::uppercase;
            std::cout << "ID: 0x" << msg.ID
                      << (msg.MSGTYPE & PCAN_MESSAGE_EXTENDED ? " (EFF)" : "")
                      << (msg.MSGTYPE & PCAN_MESSAGE_RTR ? " (RTR)" : "")
                      << "  DLC: " << static_cast<int>(msg.LEN) << "  Data: ";
            for (int i = 0; i < msg.LEN; ++i)
                std::cout << std::setw(2) << std::setfill('0')
                          << static_cast<int>(msg.DATA[i]) << ' ';
            std::cout << std::dec << std::nouppercase << '\n';
        } else if (status != PCAN_ERROR_QRCVEMPTY) {
            char err[256];
            CAN_GetErrorText(status, 0x09, err);
            std::cerr << "CAN_Read error: " << err << '\n';
            break;
        }
        // else: queue empty → just loop again (you may add Sleep(1) to avoid busy‑wait)
    }

    CAN_Uninitialize(PCAN_USBBUS1);
    return 0;
}
```

**Build (Visual Studio command prompt)**

```cmd
cl /EHsc /I"C:\Program Files\PEAK-System\PCAN-Basic" read_pcan.cpp ^
   "C:\Program Files\PEAK-System\PCAN-Basic\PCANBasic.lib"
```

Run the resulting `read_pcan.exe`. The API is almost identical to the Linux socket version, just wrapped in the PCAN‑Basic functions.

