If you run the client again **with the same sequence number** (e.g. by forcing a retry), the server will **not** process the payload again – it will just resend the ACK.

You can also test loss by adding a simple `iptables` rule or by using `tc` to drop packets; the client will automatically retry until it gets the ACK or hits the retry limit.

