## 7️⃣ Service Layer – `TransactionService.java`

```java
package com.example.cognivault.service;

import com.example.cognivault.model.TransactionRequest;
import com.example.cognivault.model.TransactionResponse;
import org.apache.camel.ProducerTemplate;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Service;

/**
 * Thin façade that hides Camel from the rest of the application.
 */
@Service
public class TransactionService {

    private final ProducerTemplate producerTemplate;

    public TransactionService(ProducerTemplate producerTemplate) {
        this.producerTemplate = producerTemplate;
    }

    /**
     * Sends a transaction request to Cognivault ESB and returns the response.
     *
     * @param request the business transaction to be processed
     * @return the ESB’s response (transactionId, status, …)
     */
    public TransactionResponse submitTransaction(TransactionRequest request) {
        // The body is the POJO; Camel will marshal it to JSON as defined in the route.
        return producerTemplate.requestBody("direct:invokeCognivault", request, TransactionResponse.class);
    }
}
```

