## 4️⃣ When *true* O(1) worst‑case is required

`ConcurrentHashMap` gives **average** O(1) performance. In pathological cases (many keys colliding to the same bucket) the cost can degrade to O(n). If you truly need guaranteed worst‑case constant time, you’d have to look at specialized data structures (e.g., **Cuckoo hashing** or **perfect hash functions**) or a third‑party library such as **FastUtil** or **Koloboke**. Those libraries are not part of the JDK, but they can be added as a Maven/Gradle dependency.

