```

You can see the **first iteration** is slower (arena grows to accommodate 1 M `Point`s). Subsequent iterations are faster because the arena is simply **reset** and reused.

---

## 5. How this maps to the future **Go 1.35** API

When the official `arena` package lands in the standard library (or a later Go release) the code will look almost identical:

| Current (experimental) | Future (standard) |
|------------------------|-------------------|
| `import "golang.org/x/exp/arena"` | `import "runtime/arena"` (or `runtime/arena` – exact path TBD) |
| `a := arena.NewArena()` | `a := arena.New()` (or `arena.NewArena()`) |
| `a.New(T{})` | unchanged |
| `a.Reset()` | unchanged |
| `a.Free()` | may be unnecessary because the GC will reclaim the arena when it becomes unreachable, but the method will likely still exist for explicit release. |

So **once Go 1.35 ships**, you’ll only need to adjust the import path (and possibly rename `NewArena` → `New`). The rest of the program stays exactly the same.

---

## 6. Common pitfalls & best‑practice checklist

| ✅ Good practice | ❌ What can go wrong |
|------------------|----------------------|
| **All arena‑allocated objects are dead before `Reset`.** The GC does *not* track arena memory, so holding a reference after a reset will lead to use‑after‑free bugs. | Accidentally keeping a slice or pointer to arena data across a reset. |
| **Call `Reset` *only* when you truly want to discard everything** (e.g., after a batch, frame, request, etc.). | Resetting in the middle of a computation that still needs earlier allocations. |
| **Prefer a single long‑lived arena per logical “batch”** rather than creating a new arena each time. | Creating a new arena per request defeats the purpose of reuse and adds allocation overhead. |
| **If you need to keep some objects across resets, allocate them on the normal heap** (or use a second arena). | Mixing lifetimes in the same arena leads to subtle bugs. |
| **Run the program with `-memprofile` or `-trace`** to verify that memory usage stays bounded. | Assuming the arena works without measuring; you might be leaking via stray references. |

---

