```
Theorem: ∀ input: string, parseJson(input) ∈ JsonValue ∪ {null}
Proof:
1. Base case: empty string → returns null ✓
2. Inductive case: Assume parseJson works for all strings of length n
   For length n+1: All parsing functions are total
   - parseString always returns string (or empty)
   - parseNumber always returns number (or 0)
   - etc.
