/**
 * Theorem: For all ASTs and environments,
 * interpret(ast, env) = compileAndExecute(ast, env)
 * 
 * Proof sketch by structural induction:
 * 
 * Base cases:
 * 1. Literal n: interpret returns n, compiled code returns n ✓
 * 2. Variable x: interpret returns env(x), compiled code returns env(x) ✓
 * 
 * Inductive step:
 * Assume for subexpressions e1, e2:
 *   interpret(e1, env) = compileAndExecute(e1, env)
 *   interpret(e2, env) = compileAndExecute(e2, env)
 * 
 * For ADD(e1, e2):
 *   interpret(ADD(e1, e2), env) 
 *   = interpret(e1, env) + interpret(e2, env)          [by definition]
 *   = compileAndExecute(e1, env) + compileAndExecute(e2, env) [by IH]
 *   = compileAndExecute(ADD(e1, e2), env)             [by compilation rules]
 * 
 * Similar for other operations. QED.
 */
