/**
 * Single-decree Paxos consensus — internal reference implementation.
 *
 * <p><b>What this guarantees (safety):</b> Once a value is chosen by a
 * majority, no different value can ever be chosen. This holds even in a
 * fully asynchronous network with up to ⌊(N-1)/2⌋ crash failures.
 *
 * <p><b>What this does NOT guarantee (liveness):</b> Per the FLP
 * impossibility result, no deterministic protocol can guarantee
 * termination in a purely asynchronous model with even one crash.
 * In practice, Paxos terminates under partial synchrony (eventual
 * message delivery + bounded processing). The timeouts in this
 * implementation are a stand-in for that assumption.
 *
 * <p>Each node plays all three roles (Proposer, Acceptor, Learner).
 * Requires Java 17+ for sealed interfaces.
