/**
 * Hash64: A 64-bit hash function in the style of SipHash-2-4.
 *
 * <p>This class provides a fast, deterministic 64-bit hash suitable for
 * hash tables, checksums, and similar non-cryptographic uses. It is
 * <strong>not</strong> a substitute for SHA-256 in security-critical
 * contexts; its 64-bit output is too small to resist brute-force search.
 *
 * <p>The construction is a Merkle–Damgård iteration of a 256-bit
 * compression function built from the SipRound permutation.
